 "notes": [
  "AS ORIGINALLY REPORTED: quarter ended 30-Jun-2026, before the Mobility spin-off (completed 1-Jul-2026; Mobility Global, NYSE: MBGL). Exhibit 1 and Exhibit 4 still include Mobility as a segment; no discontinued operations in the reported statements.",
  "Segment formerly 'Commodity Insights' is published as 'Energy' (code CI). Segment order in the release changed to Ratings, Indices, Energy, Market Intelligence, Mobility.",
  "The release publishes NO as-reported (with-Mobility) adjusted figures: adjusted OP / NI / EPS are only on a pro forma (ex-Mobility, recast) basis (Exhibit 6) -> recorded under pro_forma; ngaap.adj_op / adj_ni / adj_eps and segment adj_op are omitted here.",
  "Segment nongaap: Ratings 8, Indices 3, Energy 15, Market Intelligence 20 are the 'Non-GAAP adjustments' printed in Exhibit 6 (same footnote items as Exhibit 4 (a)-(d)); Mobility 21 = the single Exhibit 4 footnote (e) item. Footnote sums: Indices 2 (computed) vs 3 printed; Energy 17 (computed) vs 15 printed; MI 20 ties.",
  "Corporate as-reported footnote (f) items sum to 57 pre-tax (computed: 56 - 11 + 11 + 1); no as-reported corporate adjusted figure printed, so corp_nongaap / adj_corp omitted.",
  "Deal-related amortization by segment from Exhibit 4 footnotes; total 275 (computed) equals Exhibit 5 'Historical' amortization of intangibles 275. No as-reported deal-amortization tax / after-tax printed.",
  "ngaap.items: pre-tax from Exhibit 4 footnotes; after-tax ('net') taken from the Exhibit 6 footnotes where the identical item and pre-tax amount is listed (none for Mobility). Corporate disposition-related costs: $56 million pre-tax, $104 million after-tax as printed (after-tax exceeds pre-tax).",
  "is.op_rel / sga / dep / amort come from the 'Historical' column of Exhibit 5 (three months); they sum to Expenses 2,345.",
  "Exhibit 1 prints 'Other income, net' = (4), i.e. income -> oth_inc = 4. Gain on dispositions 11 (corporate).",
  "Organic: the consolidated organic table is pro forma (ex-Mobility) -> pro_forma.organic. Ratings and Indices organic tables use GAAP revenue (unchanged by the recast) and are recorded here too.",
  "FCF adjusting items use the 2026 labels. Cash flow is six months year to date, as reported (includes Mobility); three-month FCF from Exhibit 8 recorded with _q suffix. Capex and NCI distributions recorded as positive costs.",
  "Guidance: new 2026 outlook excludes Mobility; GAAP guidance is for continuing operations. Exhibit 9 GAAP-to-adjusted EPS reconciliation: deal-related amortization 2.00, gain on sale from divestitures (1.20), premium amortization benefit (0.06), tax rate and other 0.41. Not comparable with earlier 2026 guidance (which included Mobility).",
  "Balance sheet at 30-Jun-2026 still includes Mobility (spin completed the next day). Held-for-sale items relate to Energy's geoscience and petroleum engineering software portfolio."
 ],
