 "pro_forma": {
  "basis": "Article 11 pro forma, continuing operations excluding Mobility (as if the Separation occurred 1-Jan-2023; transaction accounting adjustments as if 1-Jan-2025); segments recast for the 451 Research / Maritime & Trade transfer from MI to Energy and new corporate allocation methodology. Three months ended 30-Jun-2026.",
  "notes": [
   "is = Exhibit 5 Pro Forma column; columns = Exhibit 5 bridge (Historical, Mobility Discontinued Operations, Continuing Operations subtotal, Transaction Accounting Adjustments, Pro Forma). TAA = Transition Services Agreement reducing S&G by 6 (note b), tax 1 (note c).",
   "Mobility discontinued-operations operating profit (61) differs from Mobility segment operating profit (104): general corporate overhead previously allocated to Mobility stays in continuing operations, and separation costs move into discontinued operations.",
   "seg = Exhibit 6: rev (GAAP), *_transfers (a: product transfers MI -> Energy, Credit Analytics expenses MI -> Ratings), *_alloc (b: reallocation of costs formerly allocated to Mobility and enterprise-allocation changes), *_recast (pro forma recast), nongaap (OP add-back sign), deal_amort, adj_exp / adj_op (pro forma non-GAAP adjusted). Expense-side signs are as printed in the expense table (positive = adds expense); OP-side as printed in the OP table.",
   "Corporate: unallocated expense 104, allocation changes (59), transaction accounting adjustments (6) -> pro forma recast 39; Non-GAAP adjustments (g) printed +5 in the expense table (OP add-back -5); deal-related amortization 2; adjusted 42.",
   "Exhibit 6 does not tie exactly (company rounding): e.g. Ratings 907 + 8 + 1 = 916 vs 917 printed; Indices 373 - 4 = 369 vs 370 recast; segment pro forma recast OP 907+370+247+271-39 = 1,756 vs 1,757; segment non-GAAP adjustments 8+3+15+20-5 = 41 vs 42 printed (computed).",
   "RELEASE DOES NOT TIE (pro forma non-GAAP footnotes): footnote (g) corporate items total 63 pre-tax / 110 after-tax (computed) vs corporate Non-GAAP adjustments of -5 (OP add-back) printed; all footnote items after tax sum to 141 (computed) vs aggregate 'Non-GAAP adjustments' of 75 ($0.25) printed. The aggregate is consistent with the tables: pre-tax 42 (OP) - 6 (interest) = 36, tax on adjustments -40 -> 76 (rounding to 75). Use the aggregate lines.",
   "Non-GAAP net income reconciliation starts from pro forma net income from continuing operations attributable to S&P Global (1,205; $4.08).",
   "Exhibit 6 effective tax rates (3M): GAAP 23.5%, pro forma 21.9%, pro forma non-GAAP adjusted 19.8%.",
   "rev_type = Exhibit 7 'Adjusted (As Recast)/Pro Forma Revenue by Type' (three months)."
  ],
